diff --git a/crates/rightkit-automation/CHANGELOG.md b/crates/rightkit-automation/CHANGELOG.md
index 5ae2e33..b936a40 100644
--- a/crates/rightkit-automation/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/crates/rightkit-automation/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -1,5 +1,19 @@
 # Changelog
 
+## 0.4.5 (unreleased)
+
+Additive; no existing signature changes. Code-only: nothing here was compiled or run when written, so the Windows and macOS CI runs are the verification. Requested in rightkit#360 (HeardRight), #412 and #689 (Pulse) and #434 (SwiftRight).
+
+- **Fixed (Windows): `win::input::RawInput::key_down`, `key_up` and `key_press` fill the hardware scan code (#689).** `wScan` is now `MapVirtualKeyW(vk, MAPVK_VK_TO_VSC)`, so a receiving window that maps keys by scan code (WezTerm) sees the key. It was 0, and `SendInput` does not derive it. New `win::scan_for_vk(vk)` returns the value; `RawInput::with_scan(0)` restores the old behaviour, `with_scan(n)` forces a code. `vk::DUMMY` and any key without a scan code stay 0. The extended (`E0`) bit is unchanged.
+- **New (Windows): `win::uia::El` checked reads (#360).** `try_pid() -> Result<Option<u32>, UiaError>`, `try_native_hwnd() -> Result<Option<isize>, UiaError>`, `try_control_type() -> Result<i32, UiaError>`, plus `control_type()`, `control_type_name()`, `framework_id()` (UIA `FrameworkId`, so XAML/WinUI fields can be told from Win32) and `supports_text_edit()` (`TextEditPattern` probe; `Some(false)` is a positive answer, `None` means UIA could not say). `UiaError::{ElementNotAvailable, ElementNotEnabled, Failed(hresult)}` keeps "the element is gone" (`UIA_E_ELEMENTNOTAVAILABLE`) apart from "UIA failed". The existing `Option` readers are unchanged.
+- **Fixed (Windows): the UIA error mapping used wrong `HRESULT` values.** `UIA_E_NOTSUPPORTED` is `0x80040204` and `UIA_E_ELEMENTNOTAVAILABLE` is `0x80040201`; the old table swapped them, so an unavailable element surfaced as `Error::Unsupported` instead of `Error::NotFound`.
+- **New (Windows): `win::region` (#412).** `capture_region(Rect) -> RegionImage` copies a rectangle of the virtual desktop (every app, as the user sees it) with `BitBlt` and `CAPTUREBLT`, clipped to the desktop; `capture_region_png(Rect, path)` writes a PNG; `virtual_screen()` gives the bounds. No redaction and no policy: the caller owns what may be captured.
+- **New (macOS): `macos::capture_region_png(Rect, path) -> Result<(u32, u32)>` (#412).** The same for macOS, in global display points with a top-left origin, through `CGWindowListCreateImage`; needs Screen Recording permission. Returns the pixel size written.
+- **New (Windows): `win::clipboard` (#412).** `ClipboardListener::start(callback)` registers a hidden message-only window with `AddClipboardFormatListener` on its own thread and calls back with a `ClipboardChange { sequence, formats }` for every change; dropping or `stop()` removes it and joins the thread. `list_formats()` and `read_raw(&ReadLimits) -> RawClipboard` return every format (or `ReadLimits::only`) as raw bytes with a per-format and a total byte limit (`FormatData::{Bytes, TooLarge, Handle, Unreadable}`). GDI-handle formats are reported as `Handle`; `cf::*` and `standard_format_name` name the standard ids. No policy: the caller decides what may be read or kept.
+- **New (Windows): `win::dropfiles` (#412).** `drop_files(hwnd, &[&Path], x, y)` posts `WM_DROPFILES` with a `DROPFILES` block to a window that set `WS_EX_ACCEPTFILES` (`accepts_files(hwnd)`), as if dropped from Explorer, with no cursor, focus or `SendInput`. A window that takes drops through OLE is refused with `Error::Unsupported`. A higher-integrity target ignores the message unless it allowed it (UIPI).
+- **New (Windows): `win::ime` (#434, IME part).** `compose(hwnd, text)`, `commit(hwnd)`, `cancel(hwnd)` drive the input context of a window of the calling process with IMM32, and `candidate_rect(hwnd) -> Option<Rect>` finds the visible IME candidate window of any process by window class. Win32 has no setter for the cursor inside a composition string, so `compose` takes no cursor argument. Cargo features `Win32_UI_Input_Ime` and `Win32_System_LibraryLoader` are now enabled for the `windows` crate (no new dependency).
+- **Already present, no change:** media and system keys (`send_media_key`, #290), `sensitive` checksum detectors and the Pulse word lists (#412 first part, #529), `win::set_window_frame` and macOS `ax::El::set_point` / `set_size` / `set_frame` for moving and resizing another app's window (#412, #188), the caller event marker (`marker`, #188), `capture_safety` (#177), `win::dialog::task_dialog_click` and `win::msaa::default_action` (#434), and the AX attribute path that ignores the interaction switches (`ax::El::attribute`, #244).
+
 ## 0.4.4 (2026-10-17)
 
 Breaking only for code that reached into `win::uia::El`'s public field; otherwise additive. Code-only: nothing in this section was compiled or run when written (the Windows items need a Windows build and run), so the Windows CI run is the verification. Requested in rightkit#360 (HeardRight full UIA cutover).
